index 00000000..f30dfbb1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/671-plasma-post.md
@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+## #671 - a PathPilot plasma post for the Tormach 1300PL
+
+Sources (clean room, behaviour only): Tormach's *1300PL Operator's Manual*
+UM10720 v1223A - §6.2.1-6.2.2 (the test program and its code breakdown,
+pp. 50-51), §6.3-6.3.1 (AutoFS, the hand-stated block, pp. 51-52), §7.1
+(G15, G16, p. 54), §7.2 (M200-M213, pp. 54-55) - and Tormach's *PathPilot
+Post Processor Guidelines* knowledge-base page (its Plasma column). No
+Autodesk/Fusion post, no vendor post script and no CAM output was read.
+
+**1. Every word, from its source.**
+
+| word | meaning | source |
+|---|---|---|
+| `G20` / `G21` | the unit, from the machine (`machine.units`) | [PG] G20/G21 supported on plasma |
+| `G90 G91.1 G94 G17 G40 G49 G80` | absolute, incremental arc centres, feed/min, XY, no comp, no length offset, no cycle - stated once | [PG] each supported on plasma; [UM] §6.2.2 "resets the modal state" |
+| `G64 P0.005 Q0.005` | path blending, P in INCHES even on a G21 program | [UM] §6.2.1 (the numbers); [PG] "G64 must be specified in inch units" |
+| `G54`.. | the work offset | [UM] §6.2.1 |
+| `G43 H1` | the torch's length offset, always H1 | [PG] "For plasma, this should always be set to H1"; [UM] §6.2.2 Tool 1 is the torch |
+| `G30` | the operator's G30 height (and position) - after the preamble, after every `M205`, and at the end | [UM] §6.2.1-6.2.2 ("Initial Move", program end) |
+| `G0 X Y` | rapid to the pierce point - X and Y only | [UM] §6.2.1 `G0 X0 Y0`; §6.3 the control owns Z |
+| `M200` | AutoFS: feed, THC volts, pierce height, pierce delay, amps from the material picked in PathPilot | [UM] §6.3, §7.2 |
+| `M207 P` / `M208 P` / `M209 P` | pierce height / cut height (program unit) / pierce delay (s) - written after `M200` only when the op states them | [UM] §6.3.1, §7.2 ("Set by M200: Yes") |
+| `G15` | probe down to the plate; the WCS Z is set to 0 there | [UM] §7.1 |
+| `G16` | rise to the pierce height, fire, wait the delay, cut height, THC on | [UM] §7.1 |
+| `G1` / `G2` / `G3` X Y [I J] [F] | the cut, XY only | [PG] G1/G2/G3 supported; F in/min or mm/min per G20/G21 |
+| `G41.1 D` / `G42.1 D` / `G40` | control compensation, D = the kerf (diameter), on its own line ahead of the straight lead | [PG] G41.1/G42.1 supported on plasma (its G42.1 "left side" text is a copy slip) |
+| `M205` | torch off, Z back to the G30 height | [UM] §7.2 |
+| `M30` | program end; no `%` fence, no `;` | [PG] M30 supported; "no $ or %" |
+
+**2. M200 always, the stated numbers after it.** `M200` also supplies the
+THC voltage and the amperage, which the op never states, so it is written
+for every contour; a stated pierce height, cut height or delay follows it
+as `M207`/`M208`/`M209` (M200 sets all three, so the later word wins).
+*Dropped:* the §6.3.1 hand-stated block alone (M210/M211/M207-M209 + F) -
+it needs THC volts and amps the op does not have. `M203` (Start Torch) is
+not used: `G16` strikes the arc after the probe. `M210`-`M213` never.
+
+**3. No M6.** The manual's test program writes `T1 M6 G43 H1`; the
+guidelines list M6 (and T only as M6's argument) as unsupported on
+plasma. The post writes `G43 H1` alone - nothing to change on a one-torch
+table. *Open, for the Hub run:* does PathPilot plasma accept or need
+`T1 M6`?
+
+**4. G30 after every M205.** As the issue specified and the manual's
+program end does. M205 already returns Z to the G30 height; whether the
+bare `G30` also moves X and Y to the stored G30 position (LinuxCNC's
+G30 does) is for the Hub run - a per-contour XY trip home would cost
+time, never safety (the torch travels at the G30 height). *Dropped:*
+omitting it between contours (keeps the issue's block exact until the
+Hub says otherwise).
+
+**5. G41.1/G42.1 D<kerf>, not G41/G42.** The dynamic form states the kerf
+the CL was planned with, so the tool table's torch diameter can never
+silently disagree with the path; the engage and `G40` cancel each stand on
+their own line before the straight lead #670 guarantees (≥ the kerf
+radius, PathPilot's entry rule). Wear compensation is refused by name.
+
+**6. Z is the control's.** No Z word is ever written: rapids name only the
+next pierce point (a rapid that changes only Z is dropped), and a lit move
+that changes Z is refused by name ("a Z cutting move"). The `.cl` cut
+plane is the generator's model, not a program word.
+
+**7. Small holes under AutoFS.** With the op's feed blank (`AUTOFEED`, the
+default), the lit moves carry no F and the small-hole rule's 65 % cannot
+be applied to a feed the program never knows; the hole posts at the
+AutoFS feed with a comment saying so (`SMALL HOLE AT THE AUTOFS FEED`).
+*Dropped:* refusing it (it would block every default plate with a hole -
+a quality loss, not a gouge); reading AutoFS's feed variable (not public).
+With a stated feed the CL already carries the reduced F.
+
+**8. The stream carries the torch.** New `.cnc` records `PLASMA ...` and
+`TORCH ON|OFF ...`, spelled exactly as the `.cl` v5 records minus the
+`; ` - one reader (`cl::parse_*`) takes both, so the committed `.cl`
+golden posts as it stands. `dump` writes the header before `SECTION` (a
+plasma post knows at `onSection`) and wraps each span around its records,
+the ON ahead of a G41/G42 engage and the OFF after the cancel's lead-out.
+New hooks `onPlasma`, `onTorchOn`, `onTorchOff`; the engine keeps the torch
+law (no torch without a header, no ON while lit, no rapid while lit, no
+section left lit) and refuses a script without the torch hooks - which is
+how every milling post declines a plasma path. *Dropped:* PARAM-only
+headers (a PARAM cannot carry the per-contour spans) and a new
+`ENGAGE`-style motion record (the moves stay the torch-centre truth).
+
+**9. The machine says plasma.** `machine.kind` (new script property, the
+declared kind's word through either door) must be `plasma`, or the post
+refuses by name; a stated rotary, an rpm, a coolant ask other than Off,
+a cycle and a tilted move are refused by name too. The 1300PL .mch states
+no `safe_retract` - this post never writes G53; G30 is its retract.
+
+**10. Registry.** "Tormach PathPilot Plasma" is appended to `BUILTINS`
+(entry 0 stays Fanuc) and is `PLASMA_POSTS`' only entry: offered for a
+plasma table (`default_post_for`, the Setup pane's offer) and never for a
+mill, lathe or mill-turn; no milling post serves the 1300PL.
+
+**Not exercised:** a PathPilot Hub (1300PL simulator) run and a real cut.
+The program must be loaded on the Hub before anyone trusts it on a machine.

From 452306af2a2fa4b04bb3e642e6b0a16edd3c3349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:41:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(post): pin every plasma refusal; a pending kerf comp
 never outlives its torch span (#679 review)

The six tormach-plasma.cps refusals no test reached (dark, comp-open,
comparc, nofeed, plane, wear) each get a refused(...) case in
plasma_post_refusals; deleting any one now fails the suite.

A G41.1/G42.1 still pending when the torch goes out (COMP read, no lit
straight G1 carried it) is refused by name ("comp-pending") and the
word is dropped at TORCH OFF, so it can never land on the next
contour's first G1. Pinned by
a_pending_kerf_engage_never_outlives_its_torch_span.

TORCH SMALL's range error now names the factor's range, (0, 1], and
the SMALL word's x1000 scale; pinned by
a_small_hole_factor_out_of_range_names_the_factor_range.

Goldens unchanged.

Refs #671

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
---
 assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps          |  9 ++++
 crates/app/tests/plasma_post_refusals.rs | 67 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 crates/post/src/post/cnc_torch.rs        |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps b/assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps
index b9a888a5..98f717e0 100644
--- a/assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps
+++ b/assets/posts/tormach-plasma.cps
@@ -203,8 +203,17 @@ function onTorchOn() {
 // M205 puts the torch out and returns Z to the G30 height (§7.2); G30
 // follows it, as the issue's per-contour block and the manual's own
 // program end (§6.2.1) write it.
+// A compensation word never outlives its torch span: an engage still
+// pending here (COMP read, no lit straight G1 carried it) breaks the
+// stream's law - the engage rides inside the span, ahead of its lead -
+// so it is refused by name, and dropped either way so it can never land
+// on the next contour's first G1 (a small hole the computer already
+// offset would take the kerf twice).
 function onTorchOff() {
+  var engage = compWord !== "" && compWord !== "G40";
+  compWord = "";
   if (!plasmaOk()) { lit = false; return; }
+  if (engage) refuse("comp-pending" + opName, who() + "the torch goes out with a G41/G42 engage no lit straight move carried - the kerf compensation would land on the next contour");
   if (compOn) refuse("comp-open" + opName, who() + "the torch goes out under G41/G42 - the compensation was never cancelled");
   block(["M205"]);
   block(["G30"]);
diff --git a/crates/app/tests/plasma_post_refusals.rs b/crates/app/tests/plasma_post_refusals.rs
index f2ad6fff..1224d716 100644
--- a/crates/app/tests/plasma_post_refusals.rs
+++ b/crates/app/tests/plasma_post_refusals.rs
@@ -1,7 +1,9 @@
 //! #671: what the PathPilot plasma post refuses by name - a non-plasma
 //! op, a Plasma Profile path with no plasma record, a spindle rpm, a
 //! rotary, a coolant ask, a Z cutting move, a canned cycle, a machine
-//! that is not a plasma table - and what the engine refuses for any
+//! that is not a plasma table, a feed with the torch off, a lit move with
+//! no feed, an arc outside XY, G41/G42 left open at TORCH OFF, engaged on
+//! an arc or still pending, wear compensation - and what the engine refuses for any
 //! post (a torch with no header, an ON while lit, a torch never put
 //! out, a rapid while lit, a mill post handed torch records); and the
 //! registry: offered for the 1300PL, never for a mill, and the mills'
@@ -59,6 +61,7 @@ fn section(extra: &str, header: &str, cut: &str) -> String {
 
 const CUT: &str = "Feed X 10000 Y 0 Z 6000 F 2500000\nFeed X 10000 Y 10000 Z 6000 F 2500000\n";
 const HEAD: &str = "PLASMA KERF1500\n";
+const CONTROL: &str = "PLASMA KERF1500 CONTROL\n";
 
 #[test]
 fn a_clean_section_posts_and_every_mill_golden_is_refused_by_name() {
@@ -85,6 +88,37 @@ fn the_post_refuses_what_a_plasma_table_cannot_say() {
     refused(&section("", HEAD, &format!("{CUT}CYCLE DRILL X 0 Y 0 Z -1000 R 2000\n")), "a canned cycle");
     // A G41/G42 span under a computer offset.
     refused(&section("", HEAD, &format!("COMP LEFT 750\n{CUT}COMP OFF\n")), "the stream disagrees with its own plasma header");
+    // A feed outside any TORCH span: the engine's law does not see it,
+    // the script is the only guard against cutting with the torch off.
+    refused(
+        &section("", HEAD, CUT).replace("TORCH OFF C0\n", "TORCH OFF C0\nFeed X 0 Y 0 Z 6000 F 2500000\n"),
+        "a cutting move with the torch off",
+    );
+    // A lit move with no feed while the op states one (no AUTOFEED).
+    refused(&section("", HEAD, "Feed X 10000 Y 0 Z 6000\n"), "a lit move states no feed while the op states one");
+    // An arc outside XY (I K names the XZ plane).
+    refused(
+        &section("", HEAD, "Arc CCW X 10000 Y 0 Z 6000 F 2500000 I 5000 K 6000\n"),
+        "a plasma cut is flat",
+    );
+    // Under control compensation: the torch put out with G41/G42 still
+    // in force, an engage on an arc, and wear compensation.
+    refused(
+        &section("", CONTROL, &format!("COMP LEFT 750\n{CUT}")),
+        "the torch goes out under G41/G42 - the compensation was never cancelled",
+    );
+    refused(
+        &section(
+            "",
+            CONTROL,
+            &format!("COMP LEFT 750\nArc CCW X 10000 Y 0 Z 6000 F 2500000 I 5000 J 0\n{CUT}COMP OFF\nFeed X 9000 Y 10000 Z 6000 F 2500000\n"),
+        ),
+        "G41/G42 engages or cancels on an arc",
+    );
+    refused(
+        &section("", CONTROL, &format!("COMP LEFT 750 WEAR\n{CUT}COMP OFF\nFeed X 9000 Y 10000 Z 6000 F 2500000\n")),
+        "wear compensation is not a plasma mode",
+    );
     // The machine: a mill, or a plasma table that grew a rotary.
     let vmc: Value = serde_json::from_str(&read("assets/machines/3axis-vmc.mch")).expect("json");
     let w = warnings(script(PLASMA), &vmc, &section("", HEAD, CUT));
@@ -110,6 +144,37 @@ fn the_engine_refuses_a_torch_stream_that_cannot_mean_what_it_says() {
     refused(&section("", "PLASMA KERF1500\nPLASMA KERF1500\n", CUT), "a second PLASMA header");
 }
 
+#[test]
+fn a_pending_kerf_engage_never_outlives_its_torch_span() {
+    // COMP LEFT read after the last lit straight move: no G1 carried
+    // the G41.1, so it is refused by name at TORCH OFF - and dropped, so
+    // the next contour's first G1 never takes it.
+    let stream = section("", CONTROL, &format!("{CUT}COMP LEFT 750\n")).replace(
+        "ENDSECTION\n",
+        "TORCH ON C1 OUTER\nFeed X 20000 Y 0 Z 6000 F 2500000\nFeed X 20000 Y 10000 Z 6000 F 2500000\nTORCH OFF C1\nENDSECTION\n",
+    );
+    let out = engine::run(script(PLASMA), &pl1300(), &stream).expect("the engine runs; the post refuses");
+    assert!(
+        out.warnings.iter().any(|m| m.contains("a G41/G42 engage no lit straight move carried")),
+        "{:?}",
+        out.warnings
+    );
+    assert!(!out.program.contains("G41.1"), "the pending engage leaked onto C1:\n{}", out.program);
+    // A cancel with its lead-out posts clean, and the engage is written.
+    let clean = section("", CONTROL, &format!("COMP LEFT 750\n{CUT}COMP OFF\nFeed X 9000 Y 10000 Z 6000 F 2500000\n"));
+    let out = engine::run(script(PLASMA), &pl1300(), &clean).expect("runs");
+    assert!(out.warnings.is_empty(), "{:?}", out.warnings);
+    assert!(out.program.contains("G41.1 D"), "{}", out.program);
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn a_small_hole_factor_out_of_range_names_the_factor_range() {
+    let e = engine::run(script(PLASMA), &pl1300(), &section("", HEAD, CUT).replace("TORCH ON C0 OUTER", "TORCH ON C0 OUTER SMALL1500"))
+        .map(|o| o.warnings.join("; "))
+        .unwrap_or_else(|e| e.to_string());
+    assert!(e.contains("a feed factor in (0, 1]"), "{e}");
+}
+
 #[test]
 fn the_mills_posts_decline_a_plasma_stream_and_the_1300pl() {
     let stream = read("crates/app/tests/golden/plasma_plate_with_holes.cl");
